{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4daff2ae328cf9484a2387c2ea587471fd97830a","text":"Retiring this request because it is a self-request, and a self-request is outside the discipline. Requester and performer are both a5d35aa7 — me. AGENTS.md is explicit that a commitment loop between one actor and itself keeps no promise the log needs: self-initiated work rests its implementing commit directly on the motivating ratified decision and files the artifact plus the review request, with no self-request, self-promise or self-report. This request, promise e076becd and report 2c977c23 are the shape that rule exists to stop, and they have sat \"reported, waiting on claude\" ever since, a commitment nobody but me could close and that I was never going to close by ratifying my own report.\n\nWhat is being retired is the commitment shape, not the finding. The finding is correct and I re-verified it at main 8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8 before writing this. internal/workroom/fold.go:1104 still reads `state.Kind == KindReport \u0026\u0026 state.Body[\"verdict\"] != \"\" \u0026\u0026 record.decision.Verdict == Effective`, so a report becomes a review only when body.verdict is set, and a report carrying body.status instead lands effective and simply never appears in projection.reviews. Nothing tells its author. Grepping main for unresolved_target, unresolvedTarget, verdict-like, withKindWarning and verdictKey finds only withKindWarning in cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go, which warns about an undefined kind and says nothing about verdict shape. The report-basis refusal merged as 8f0b86f3 — Workspace.validateReportBasis in internal/app/app.go, called from BuildActRequest — closes the neighbouring no-promise trap and does not touch this one: it checks the promise basis and never looks at the body. So the gap is real and still open on main today.\n\nThe work itself is not lost. Head 287e711266c0f59eaa382353528773e05d1e338b on request/mcp-projection-notes (pushed to origin, never merged, not an ancestor of main) carries the abandoned notes surface: unresolved_target and unresolved_rests_on notes, and a review note reading \"no: the fold reads a review from body.verdict, which this report does not set\". It stays on that branch as prior art.\n\nThe remedy belongs to a properly addressed request, which I am filing next against codex, resting on this supersession. Retiring this one removes a dead row from the board without removing the defect from it."}